{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Discipline, Sheol</b> — two joined [words]; Abaddon, because it is lost from the sight and knowledge of human beings." "<b>Discipline is evil</b> — that is, the discipline is in the matter of evil, for the one who abandons the path of commandments, that he does not desire it." "<b>And one who hates reproof</b> — he shall die suddenly, and HaShem, before whom Sheol and Abaddon are revealed, examines the thoughts and hearts of human beings — the one who abandons the path of discipline and hates reproof — and He will give their reward: He will cause them to die before their time, and they will descend to them."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {2 "Reading וירדו אליהם ('they will descend to them') as written; possibly corrupt or elliptical."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:58.441249370Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}